 ### Full Normalization Pipeline
-Combines camera-based similarity normalization and principal axes alignment. First, a similarity transform $T_1$ is computed from cameras using `similarity_from_cameras`. Cameras and points are transformed by $T_1$. Then, a principal axes transform $T_2$ is computed from the transformed points (using PCA). Cameras and points are transformed by $T_2$. The final transform is $T_2 @ T_1$. This ensures both camera-centric alignment and data-centric principal axis alignment. [S1, unofficial]
